Assistance during braking manoeuvr in critical situations is now mandatory
Like already in the anti-lock braking system ABS and as is happening precisely now with ESP stability control, the auxiliary aid systems in emergencies in emergencies have to become a mandatory equipment in European vehicles in emergencies.
In reality they are already compulsory for all newly registered passenger vehicles and small sewage vans, a waiting period has been determined until the end of February 2011 for the remaining vehicles.
Adopted by the European Union, the aim is to improve the conservation of pedestrian fugues, however these braking systems can also help to prevent many chamoo accidents because of their way.
The task of emergency brake help is to exert greater pressure on the brakes during a critical braking manoeuvre, which recognizes the brake pedal based on the brake thickness executed by the driver.
However this system doesn’t exercise this pressure until cluding the conclusion.
According to an examination commissioned by the component manufacturer for the component vehicles, a thousand who were involved in an accident didn't even come to stepping on the brake pedal before reaction and half of them hadn't briced at full strength.
Up to 1,100 accident accursances
The brake aid, on the other hand, intervenes in the braking system with a maximum force, thereby reducing the braking time and thus the brake distance, which a car traverses during braking.
According to an EU study every year up to 1,100 deadly accident acres could be avoided damage each year when all vehicles were equipped with this type of emergency brake assistant.
There would even fewer accidents be caused to prevent every fourth accident involving personal injuries as soon as the so-called smart emergency braking systems become very popular.
The v vehicle is equipped with a system which detects obstacles (via radar or a camera) and warns the driver, while exerting a slight pressure on the brakes at the same time.
When the driver responds as a consequence, the system helps him to increase the pressure on the brake pedal when necessary.
If the driver doesn't respond to the alert and even when collision is already inevitable, the brake Assist exercises maximum pressure on brakes in order to keep damage as small as possible.
